<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexei Brusilov</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexei Brusilov was a Russian general in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. His offensive of 1916 against Austro-Hungarian forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a> inflicted very heavy losses. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brusilov-offensive">Brusilov Offensive</a> severely weakened the military of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, which became increasingly dependent on German support.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexei-brusilov.jpg" alt="Alexei Brusilov" width="288" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%91%D1%80%D1%83%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B2_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B9_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
